-- ---- s 743: Register of debenture holders ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9693 | 743 Register of debenture holders
-- src:9694 | (1) Any register of debenture holders of a company that is kept by the company must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:9695 | (a) at the company's registered office, or
-- src:9696 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
-- src:9697 | (2) A company must give notice to the registrar of the place where any such register is kept available for inspection and of any change in that place.
-- src:9698 | (3) No such notice is required if the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office.
-- src:9699 | (4) If a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by—
-- src:9700 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9701 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:9702 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
-- src:9703 | (6) References in this section to a register of debenture holders include a duplicate—
-- src:9704 | (a) of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom, or
-- src:9705 | (b) of any part of such a register.
@ref s 743 Register of debenture holders (src:9693-9705)
DECLARE `s 743(6) kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `s 743(6) a register of debenture holders`
    `s 743(6) a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom`
    `s 743(6) a duplicate of part of such a register`
    `s 743(6) something else`

-- (6) "References in this section to a register of debenture holders include a duplicate (a) of a register ... kept
-- outside the United Kingdom, or (b) of any part of such a register."  "include": the list is not closed.
@ref s 743(6) Register of debenture holders: duplicates (src:9703-9705)
GIVEN document IS A `s 743(6) kind of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743(6) the document is a register of debenture holders for this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `s 743(6) a register of debenture holders` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 743(6) a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 743(6) a duplicate of part of such a register` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 743(6) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this section to a register of debenture holders include a duplicate"

-- (1) "Any register of debenture holders of a company that is kept by the company must be kept available for
-- inspection (a) at the company's registered office, or (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136."
-- The place specified under s 1136 is another part's answer (coa25): an input, MAYBE BOOLEAN.
@ref s 743(1) Register of debenture holders: where it is kept (src:9694-9696)
GIVEN document IS A `s 743(6) kind of document`
      `the register is kept by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is kept available for inspection at a place specified in regulations under section 1136 (s 1136)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743(1) the register is kept available for inspection as the subsection requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 743(6) the document is a register of debenture holders for this section` document
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT (`the register is kept by the company`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any register of debenture holders of a company that is kept by the company"
        ELSE IF `the register is kept available for inspection at the company's registered office`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE CONSIDER `the register is kept available for inspection at a place specified in regulations under section 1136 (s 1136)`
                  WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                  WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be kept available for inspection— (a) at the company's registered office, or (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136"
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the place is one specified in regulations under section 1136 is that section's answer
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any register of debenture holders"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): see s 743(6)

-- (3) "No such notice is required if the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept
-- available for inspection at the company's registered office."  When the condition fails the exemption does not
-- apply (fork F4: a failed "if" is the text's no, within this provision).
@ref s 743(3) Register of debenture holders: no notice needed (src:9698)
GIVEN `the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743(3) the company is excused from giving the notice` MEANS
    IF `the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such notice is required if the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office"

-- (2) "A company must give notice to the registrar of the place where any such register is kept available for
-- inspection and of any change in that place."  The text states no time for the notice (fork F5).
@ref s 743(2) Register of debenture holders: notice to the registrar (src:9697)
GIVEN document IS A `s 743(6) kind of document`
      `the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection has been given to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the change in that place has been given to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743(2) the company has given the notice to the registrar as the subsection requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 743(6) the document is a register of debenture holders for this section` document
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 743(3) the company is excused from giving the notice` `the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- "No such notice is required": nothing is owing, so nothing is left undone (fork F5)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not reachable, s 743(3) answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            IF       `notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection has been given to the registrar`
                 AND ((NOT (`the place has changed`)) OR `notice of the change in that place has been given to the registrar`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar of the place where any such register is kept available for inspection and of any change in that place"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such register"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): see s 743(6)

-- The duty as a regulative rule.  No time is stated, so no WITHIN (the duty stands until it is done).
@ref s 743(2) Register of debenture holders: the duty (src:9697-9698)
DECLARE `s 743 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 743 give the registrar notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection`

@ref s 743(2) Register of debenture holders: the duty (src:9697-9698)
GIVEN `the company is excused under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 743 act`
`s 743(2) the company must give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the company is excused under subsection (3)`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Company
         MUST `s 743 give the registrar notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection`
         HENCE FULFILLED

-- (4) "If a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by (a) the
-- company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default."  The text does not say when a default begins,
-- so the number of days is an input (fork F5).
@ref s 743(4) Register of debenture holders: default for 14 days (src:9699)
GIVEN `the number of days the company has made default in complying with subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743(4) the company has made default for 14 days` MEANS
    IF `the number of days the company has made default in complying with subsection (2)` AT LEAST 14
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2)"

DECLARE `s 743(4) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 743(4) the company`
    `s 743(4) an officer of the company` HAS `s 743(4) the officer is in default (s 1121)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 743(4) another person`

@ref s 743(4) Register of debenture holders: the offence (src:9699-9701)
GIVEN document IS A `s 743(6) kind of document`
      `the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection has been given to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the change in that place has been given to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the company has made default in complying with subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
      person IS A `s 743(4) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 743(2) the company has given the notice to the registrar as the subsection requires` document `the register has, at all times since it came into existence, been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` `notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection has been given to the registrar` `the place has changed` `notice of the change in that place has been given to the registrar`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the register is not one the subsection governs
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 743(4) the company has made default for 14 days` `the number of days the company has made default in complying with subsection (2)`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2)"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not reachable, the 14-day test answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
            CONSIDER person
            WHEN `s 743(4) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 743(4) an officer of the company` inDefault THEN
                CONSIDER inDefault
                WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121
            WHEN `s 743(4) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and its officers in default

@ref s 743(5) Register of debenture holders: the penalty (src:9702)
`s 743(5) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- ---- s 744: Register of debenture holders: right to inspect and require copy -------------------------------

-- src:9706 | 744 Register of debenture holders: right to inspect and require copy
-- src:9707 | (1) Every register of debenture holders of a company must, except when duly closed, be open to the inspection—
-- src:9708 | (a) of the registered holder of any such debentures, or any holder of shares in the company, without charge, and
-- src:9709 | (b) of any other person on payment of such fee as may be prescribed.
-- src:9710 | (2) Any person may require a copy of the register, or any part of it, on payment of such fee as may be prescribed.
-- src:9711 | (3) A person seeking to exercise either of the rights conferred by this section must make a request to the company to that effect.
-- src:9712 | (4) The request must contain the following information—
-- src:9713 | (a) in the case of an individual, his name and address;
-- src:9714 | (b) in the case of an organisation, the name and address of an individual responsible for making the request on behalf of the organisation;
-- src:9715 | (c) the purpose for which the information is to be used; and
-- src:9716 | (d) whether the information will be disclosed to any other person, and if so—
-- src:9717 | (i) where that person is an individual, his name and address,
-- src:9718 | (ii) where that person is an organisation, the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on its behalf, and
-- src:9719 | (iii) the purpose for which the information is to be used by that person.
-- src:9720 | (5) For the purposes of this section a register is “duly closed” if it is closed in accordance with provision contained—
-- src:9721 | (a) in the articles or in the debentures,
-- src:9722 | (b) in the case of debenture stock in the stock certificates, or
-- src:9723 | (c) in the trust deed or other document securing the debentures or debenture stock.
-- src:9724 | The total period for which a register is closed in any year must not exceed 30 days.
-- src:9725 | (6) References in this section to a register of debenture holders include a duplicate—
-- src:9726 | (a) of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom, or
-- src:9727 | (b) of any part of such a register.
@ref s 744 Register of debenture holders: right to inspect and require copy (src:9706-9727)
DECLARE `s 744(6) kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `s 744(6) a register of debenture holders`
    `s 744(6) a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom`
    `s 744(6) a duplicate of part of such a register`
    `s 744(6) something else`

@ref s 744(6) Register of debenture holders: duplicates (src:9725-9727)
GIVEN document IS A `s 744(6) kind of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 744(6) the document is a register of debenture holders for this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `s 744(6) a register of debenture holders` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 744(6) a duplicate of a register of debenture holders that is kept outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 744(6) a duplicate of part of such a register` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 744(6) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this section to a register of debenture holders include a duplicate"

-- (5) "duly closed": closed in accordance with provision in (a) the articles or the debentures, (b) in the case of
-- debenture stock the stock certificates, (c) the trust deed or other document securing the debentures or debenture
-- stock; and "The total period for which a register is closed in any year must not exceed 30 days."  Fork F6: taken
-- as a condition of "duly closed": a register closed for more than 30 days in the year is not duly closed.
DECLARE `s 744(5) closure of the register` HAS
    `s 744(5) the register is closed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(5)(a) closed in accordance with provision in the articles or in the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(5)(b) closed in accordance with provision in the stock certificates (debenture stock)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(5)(c) closed in accordance with provision in the trust deed or other document securing the debentures or debenture stock` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(5) the total number of days the register is closed in the year` IS A NUMBER

@ref s 744(5) Register of debenture holders: duly closed (src:9720-9724)
GIVEN closure IS A `s 744(5) closure of the register`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 744(5) the register is duly closed` MEANS
    IF       closure's `s 744(5) the register is closed`
         AND (   closure's `s 744(5)(a) closed in accordance with provision in the articles or in the debentures`
              OR closure's `s 744(5)(b) closed in accordance with provision in the stock certificates (debenture stock)`
              OR closure's `s 744(5)(c) closed in accordance with provision in the trust deed or other document securing the debentures or debenture stock`)
    THEN
        IF closure's `s 744(5) the total number of days the register is closed in the year` AT MOST 30
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The total period for which a register is closed in any year must not exceed 30 days"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a register is “duly closed” if it is closed in accordance with provision contained—"

DECLARE `s 744(1) terms of inspection` IS ONE OF
    `s 744(1) open to inspection without charge`
    `s 744(1) open to inspection on payment of the prescribed fee`
    `s 744(1) not open to inspection because the register is duly closed`

-- (1) "Every register of debenture holders of a company must, except when duly closed, be open to the inspection (a)
-- of the registered holder of any such debentures, or any holder of shares in the company, without charge, and (b) of
-- any other person on payment of such fee as may be prescribed."  The amount of the fee is not in the Act.
@ref s 744(1) Register of debenture holders: inspection (src:9707-9709)
GIVEN document IS A `s 744(6) kind of document`
      closure IS A `s 744(5) closure of the register`
      `the person is the registered holder of debentures of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a holder of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 744(1) terms of inspection`
`s 744(1) the terms on which the person may inspect the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 744(6) the document is a register of debenture holders for this section` document
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 744(5) the register is duly closed` closure
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `s 744(1) not open to inspection because the register is duly closed` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every register of debenture holders of a company must, except when duly closed, be open to the inspection"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not reachable, s 744(5) answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            IF `the person is the registered holder of debentures of the company` OR `the person is a holder of shares in the company`
            THEN JUST `s 744(1) open to inspection without charge`
            ELSE JUST `s 744(1) open to inspection on payment of the prescribed fee`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every register of debenture holders of a company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): see s 744(6)

-- (2) "Any person may require a copy of the register, or any part of it, on payment of such fee as may be prescribed."
-- A grant whose gate is of the "on payment" kind: listed in the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (fork F32), not flipped, so
-- without payment it answers as ruling (b) gives, JUST FALSE; the other reading is NOTHING.
@ref s 744(2) Register of debenture holders: copy (src:9710)
GIVEN document IS A `s 744(6) kind of document`
      `the person pays the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 744(2) the person may require a copy of the register or any part of it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 744(6) the document is a register of debenture holders for this section` document
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person pays the prescribed fee`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on payment of such fee as may be prescribed"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a copy of the register"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): see s 744(6)

-- (3) "A person seeking to exercise either of the rights conferred by this section must make a request to the
-- company to that effect."
@ref s 744(3) Register of debenture holders: the request (src:9711)
GIVEN `the person has made a request to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 744(3) the person has made the request the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the person has made a request to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must make a request to the company to that effect"

-- (4) The request must contain (a) for an individual, his name and address, (b) for an organisation, the name and
-- address of an individual responsible for making the request on its behalf, (c) the purpose, (d) whether the
-- information will be disclosed to any other person and, if so, (i) for an individual his name and address, (ii) for an
-- organisation the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on its behalf, and
-- (iii) the purpose for which that person will use it.
DECLARE `s 744(4) request for the register` HAS
    `s 744(4) the person making the request is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(a) the request gives the individual's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(b) the request gives the name and address of an individual responsible for making it on behalf of the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(c) the request states the purpose for which the information is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(d) the request says whether the information will be disclosed to any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(d) the information will be disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(d)(i) the other person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(d)(i) the request gives that person's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(d)(ii) the request gives the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on behalf of that organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 744(4)(d)(iii) the request states the purpose for which that person will use the information` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 744(4) Register of debenture holders: what the request must contain (src:9712-9719)
GIVEN request IS A `s 744(4) request for the register`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 744(4) the request contains the information the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       (    IF request's `s 744(4) the person making the request is an individual`
                  THEN request's `s 744(4)(a) the request gives the individual's name and address`
                  ELSE request's `s 744(4)(b) the request gives the name and address of an individual responsible for making it on behalf of the organisation`)
         AND request's `s 744(4)(c) the request states the purpose for which the information is to be used`
         AND request's `s 744(4)(d) the request says whether the information will be disclosed to any other person`
         AND (    (NOT (request's `s 744(4)(d) the information will be disclosed to another person`))
              OR (    (    IF request's `s 744(4)(d)(i) the other person is an individual`
                           THEN request's `s 744(4)(d)(i) the request gives that person's name and address`
                           ELSE request's `s 744(4)(d)(ii) the request gives the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on behalf of that organisation`)
                   AND request's `s 744(4)(d)(iii) the request states the purpose for which that person will use the information`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The request must contain the following information"

-- ---- s 745: response to request for inspection or copy ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:9728 | 745 Register of debenture holders: response to request for inspection or copy
-- src:9729 | (1) Where a company receives a request under section 744 (register of debenture holders: right to inspect and require copy), it must within five working days either—
-- src:9730 | (a) comply with the request, or
-- src:9731 | (b) apply to the court.
-- src:9732 | (2) If it applies to the court it must notify the person making the request.
-- src:9733 | (3) If on an application under this section the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose—
-- src:9734 | (a) it shall direct the company not to comply with the request, and
-- src:9735 | (b) it may further order that the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on the application be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request, even if he is not a party to the application.
-- src:9736 | (4) If the court makes such a direction and it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose (whether made by the same person or different persons), it may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request.
-- src:9737 | The order must contain such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies.
-- src:9738 | (5) If on an application under this section the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request, the company must comply with the request immediately upon the court giving its decision or, as the case may be, the proceedings being discontinued.
@ref s 745 Register of debenture holders: response to request for inspection or copy (src:9728-9738)
DECLARE `s 745 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 745 comply with the request`
    `s 745 apply to the court`
    `s 745 notify the person who made the request`

-- (1) "Where a company receives a request under section 744 ..., it must within five working days either (a) comply
-- with the request, or (b) apply to the court."  The count of working days is an input: the caller counts them with
-- the keel's `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (fork F7).  A company that has done neither while
-- the five days are not up has not yet failed.
@ref s 745(1) Register of debenture holders: response within five working days (src:9729-9731)
GIVEN `the company has received a request under section 744` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has complied with the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the working days from receipt of the request to the day the company complied or applied, or to now if it has done neither` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745(1) the company has responded to the request in time` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has received a request under section 744`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company receives a request under section 744"
    ELSE IF `the company has complied with the request` OR `the company has applied to the court`
         THEN
             IF `the working days from receipt of the request to the day the company complied or applied, or to now if it has done neither` AT MOST 5
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within five working days either"
         ELSE
             IF `the working days from receipt of the request to the day the company complied or applied, or to now if it has done neither` AT MOST 5
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the five working days have not run out and the company has done neither yet, so there is no answer yet
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within five working days either"

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the clock counts working days from receipt (day 0).  A company that complies is
-- fulfilled; one that applies to the court must then notify the requester (s 745(2)); neither by day 5 is a breach.
@ref s 745(1) Register of debenture holders: the duty (src:9729-9732)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 745 act`
`s 745(1) the company must comply with the request or apply to the court` MEANS
    (PARTY Company
     MUST `s 745 comply with the request`
     WITHIN 5
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 745(1): the company neither complied with the request nor applied to the court within five working days")
    ROR
    (PARTY Company
     MUST `s 745 apply to the court`
     WITHIN 5
     HENCE (PARTY Company
            MUST `s 745 notify the person who made the request`
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 745(2): the company applied to the court and did not notify the person making the request")
     LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 745(1): the company neither complied with the request nor applied to the court within five working days")

-- (2) "If it applies to the court it must notify the person making the request."  A duty whose "if" is unmet
-- does not arise: not covered (fork F8).
@ref s 745(2) Register of debenture holders: notice to the requester (src:9732)
GIVEN `the company has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has notified the person making the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745(2) the company has notified the person making the request as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied to the court`
    THEN
        IF `the company has notified the person making the request`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it applies to the court it must notify the person making the request"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it applies to the court"

-- (3)(a) "If on an application under this section the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for
-- a proper purpose, (a) it shall direct the company not to comply with the request": the court's duty.
@ref s 745(3) Register of debenture holders: direction not to comply (src:9733-9734)
GIVEN `on an application under section 745 the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745(3)(a) the court shall direct the company not to comply with the request` MEANS
    IF `on an application under section 745 the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under this section the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose"

-- (3)(b) "it may further order that the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on the application be paid in whole or
-- in part by the person who made the request, even if he is not a party to the application": a power.
@ref s 745(3) Register of debenture holders: costs (src:9733-9735)
GIVEN `on an application under section 745 the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who made the request is a party to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745(3)(b) the court may order the person who made the request to pay the company's costs` MEANS
    IF `on an application under section 745 the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whether or not the person is a party: "even if he is not a party to the application"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If on an application under this section the court is satisfied"

-- (4) "If the court makes such a direction and it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other
-- requests made for a similar purpose (whether made by the same person or different persons), it may direct that the
-- company is not to comply with any such request."
@ref s 745(4) Register of debenture holders: other similar requests (src:9736)
GIVEN `the court has made a direction under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745(4) the court may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a direction under subsection (3)` AND `it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court makes such a direction and it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose"

-- "The order must contain such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies."
@ref s 745(4) Register of debenture holders: the order must identify the requests (src:9737)
GIVEN `the order contains such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745(4) the order identifies the requests to which it applies` MEANS
    IF `the order contains such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order must contain such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies"

-- (5) "If on an application under this section the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request,
-- the company must comply with the request immediately upon the court giving its decision or, as the case may be,
-- the proceedings being discontinued."
@ref s 745(5) Register of debenture holders: complying after the court's decision (src:9738)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 745` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has directed the company not to comply with the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has given its decision or the proceedings have been discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745(5) the company must comply with the request immediately` MEANS
    IF NOT (`an application has been made under section 745`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on an application under this section"
    ELSE IF `the court has directed the company not to comply with the request`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under this section the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request, the company must comply"
         ELSE IF `the court has given its decision or the proceedings have been discontinued`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the court has not yet decided and the proceedings continue, so the company's duty to comply has not yet arisen

-- ---- s 746: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy -----------------------------------------------

-- src:9739 | 746 Register of debenture holders: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy
-- src:9740 | (1) If an inspection required under section 744 (register of debenture holders: right to inspect and require copy) is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section, otherwise than in accordance with an order of the court, an offence is committed by—
-- src:9741 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9742 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:9743 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
-- src:9744 | (3) In the case of any such refusal or default the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or, as the case may be, direct that the copy required be sent to the person requesting it.
@ref s 746 Register of debenture holders: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy (src:9739-9744)
DECLARE `s 746(1) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 746(1) the company`
    `s 746(1) an officer of the company` HAS `s 746(1) the officer is in default (s 1121)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 746(1) another person`

-- (1) "If an inspection required under section 744 ... is refused or default is made in providing a copy required
-- under that section, otherwise than in accordance with an order of the court, an offence is committed by (a) the
-- company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default."
@ref s 746(1) Register of debenture holders: the offence (src:9740-9742)
GIVEN `an inspection required under section 744 is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `default is made in providing a copy required under section 744` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refusal or default is in accordance with an order of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 746(1) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 746(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF       (`an inspection required under section 744 is refused` OR `default is made in providing a copy required under section 744`)
         AND NOT (`the refusal or default is in accordance with an order of the court`)
    THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `s 746(1) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 746(1) an officer of the company` inDefault THEN
            CONSIDER inDefault
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121
        WHEN `s 746(1) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and its officers in default
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an inspection required under section 744 ... is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section, otherwise than in accordance with an order of the court, an offence is committed by"

@ref s 746(2) Register of debenture holders: the penalty (src:9743)
`s 746(2) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- (3) "In the case of any such refusal or default the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or, as the
-- case may be, direct that the copy required be sent to the person requesting it."
-- The gate is of the "in the case of" kind: listed in the name-test sweep (fork F33), not flipped, so JUST FALSE outside it.
@ref s 746(3) Register of debenture holders: the court's order (src:9744)
GIVEN `an inspection required under section 744 is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `default is made in providing a copy required under section 744` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refusal or default is in accordance with an order of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 746(3) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or direct that the copy be sent` MEANS
    IF       (`an inspection required under section 744 is refused` OR `default is made in providing a copy required under section 744`)
         AND NOT (`the refusal or default is in accordance with an order of the court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of any such refusal or default"

-- ---- s 747: offences in connection with request for or disclosure of information -------------------------------

-- src:9745 | 747 Register of debenture holders: offences in connection with request for or disclosure of information
-- src:9746 | (1) It is an offence for a person knowingly or recklessly to make in a request under section 744 (register of debenture holders: right to inspect and require copy) a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
-- src:9747 | (2) It is an offence for a person in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by that section—
-- src:9748 | (a) to do anything that results in the information being disclosed to another person, or
-- src:9749 | (b) to fail to do anything with the result that the information is disclosed to another person,
-- src:9750 | knowing, or having reason to suspect, that person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose.
-- src:9751 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:9752 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:9753 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:9754 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:9755 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 747 Register of debenture holders: offences in connection with request for or disclosure of information (src:9745-9755)
GIVEN `the person made a statement in a request under section 744` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the statement knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the statement recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 747(1) the person commits an offence by a statement in a request` MEANS
    IF       `the person made a statement in a request under section 744`
         AND `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
         AND (`the person made the statement knowingly` OR `the person made the statement recklessly`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person knowingly or recklessly to make in a request under section 744 ... a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular"

@ref s 747(2) Register of debenture holders: disclosure of information (src:9747-9750)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by section 744` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person did something that results in the information being disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to do something with the result that the information is disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew or had reason to suspect that the other person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 747(2) the person commits an offence by disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF       `the person is in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by section 744`
         AND (   `the person did something that results in the information being disclosed to another person`
              OR `the person failed to do something with the result that the information is disclosed to another person`)
         AND `the person knew or had reason to suspect that the other person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by that section ... knowing, or having reason to suspect, that person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose"

-- (3) The penalty depends on how the person is convicted: on indictment, imprisonment not exceeding two years or a
-- fine (or both); on summary conviction in England and Wales, twelve months or a fine not exceeding the statutory
-- maximum (or both); in Scotland or Northern Ireland, six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or
-- both).  A summary conviction in a place the text does not name is not covered.
@ref s 747(3) Register of debenture holders: the penalties (src:9751-9755)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 747(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 2, unit IS Years)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 12, unit IS Months)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text distinguishes England and Wales from Scotland and Northern Ireland

-- A period in months, for the seat's answer (years are twelve months; any other unit is not a number of months).
@ref s 747(3) Register of debenture holders: the term of imprisonment in months (src:9751-9755)
GIVEN period IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 747(3) the number of months in the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER period's unit
    WHEN Months THEN JUST (period's `number of units`)
    WHEN Years THEN JUST (period's `number of units` TIMES 12)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a period in days, weeks or working days is not a number of months

-- ---- s 748: time limit for claims arising from entry in register -----------------------------------------------

-- src:9756 | 748 Time limit for claims arising from entry in register
-- src:9757 | (1) Liability incurred by a company—
-- src:9758 | (a) from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of debenture holders, or
-- src:9759 | (b) from a failure to make or delete any such entry,
-- src:9760 | is not enforceable more than ten years after the date on which the entry was made or deleted or, as the case may be, the failure first occurred.
-- src:9761 | (2) This is without prejudice to any lesser period of limitation (and, in Scotland, to any rule that the obligation giving rise to the liability prescribes before the expiry of that period).
@ref s 748 Register of debenture holders: time limit for claims arising from entry in register (src:9756-9761)
GIVEN `the liability was incurred by the company from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability was incurred by the company from a failure to make or delete such an entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the entry was made or deleted or, as the case may be, the failure first occurred` IS A DATE
      `the date of enforcement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 748(1) the liability is barred by the ten-year limit` MEANS
    IF `the liability was incurred by the company from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of debenture holders` OR `the liability was incurred by the company from a failure to make or delete such an entry`
    THEN
        IF `the date of enforcement` GREATER THAN (`add years` `the date on which the entry was made or deleted or, as the case may be, the failure first occurred` 10)
        THEN JUST TRUE -- the text: "is not enforceable more than ten years after the date on which the entry was made or deleted or, as the case may be, the failure first occurred"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "more than ten years after"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Liability incurred by a company— (a) from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of debenture holders, or (b) from a failure to make or delete any such entry"

-- (2) "This is without prejudice to any lesser period of limitation (and, in Scotland, to any rule that the obligation
-- giving rise to the liability prescribes before the expiry of that period)."  The lesser period itself is outside the
-- sources, so only the preservation is encoded.
@ref s 748(2) Register of debenture holders: lesser periods preserved (src:9761)
GIVEN `there is a lesser period of limitation (or, in Scotland, a rule that the obligation prescribes before the ten years expire)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 748(2) the ten-year limit leaves a lesser period of limitation in place` MEANS
    IF `there is a lesser period of limitation (or, in Scotland, a rule that the obligation prescribes before the ten years expire)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names no lesser period
